 ## THE FREEZE, THE GUARD AND THE RUN
 
-As M8.18: a freeze block pins every file by SHA-256 in `FROZEN.json` before the go; the driver refuses to run without it, refuses any target before wave 1's controls have passed, and refuses any test longer than 2750 before the longest control has Persisted, valid. The orchestrator that starts the waves is frozen with the driver. Each job writes its own record, atomically, under its own path, the two C2a/R4 controls included, and no record overwrites another. A job that three launches leave unfinished ends its part of the run, its cause recorded, as in M8.18; a launch that ends early writes nothing that is read. The run goes in waves of at most four single-thread jobs, a job starting as another ends, and no wave starts before the one it depends on has ended:
